# banner.view: ONE band, full-colour background, rounded Powerline caps.
# Two flat fields, because a single line has no business declaring a list:
#
#   ```view:banner
#   label: ⚠ WARNING
#   content: two flaky suites, publication is blocked
#   ```
#
# `type:` (or `tone:`) on a decorator picks the colour, same file for every
# kind. SEVERAL bands are several blocks, never one list: the caps exist to
# make ONE band read as a pill, and stacking them scallops both flanks.
# The caps are U+E0B6/U+E0B4 (Powerline). A font without them shows two
# hollow boxes around the band; swap them for ▐ and ▌ if yours does not.
# The default is `info`: an undecorated @{view:banner} is a cyan NOTE band.
# The caps spend {{tone_cap}}, which the engine DERIVES from the chip filling
# the band, so they match it exactly whatever the class and whatever the
# theme. Spending {{tone}} there is off by one shade and was the bug: bold
# promotes a base-sixteen foreground to the bright slot, nothing promotes a
# background. Every COLOUR fills a band: the severities (warning, error,
# success, info, warn, fail, pass, high, med, low) and the plain names alike
# (red, green, yellow, cyan, orange, gold, key, dim). What has no chip is
# furniture (`code`, `box_rule`) and a host's own foreground tag: name one and
# the band vanishes, leaving two solid caps around bare text. Do not.
@tone info
{{tone_cap}}{{/}}{{tone_bg}} ${label}  ${content} {{/}}{{tone_cap}}{{/}}
